{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "23da85d5-2c37-8eef-9bdd-287a10ebc46a",
  "created_at": "2026-02-18T12:07:12-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Canvassing",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Maria T. Moniz",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Walter Tavares",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:03:01-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Canvassing, this is Walter. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:03:05-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yes, good afternoon. I'm calling about registering to vote. Well, actually, it's for my niece, no wait, she's not my niece, she's my stepdaughter's friend, she rents a room from us. Sorry. Let me start over."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:03:18-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's fine, take your time. Who is it that needs to register?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:03:23-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A student. She goes to school here in Newport and lives in a dorm during the year. She wants to know if she can register using the campus address."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:03:34-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, a student can generally register at the address where they actually live while at school, and that can be a dorm. The key is that it's where she lives now and considers her residence, not just a mailing address. Is she a U.S. citizen?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:03:50-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, she is. She's from Connecticut originally. Oh, but she'd be okay with that? Her parents' address is still on her license."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:03:58-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "She would choose one place to be registered. If she registers here, she'd be taken off the Connecticut rolls, so she can't be registered in both. That's her choice to make."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:04:09-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. And what ID does she need? Do they ask for it when she registers, or only when she votes? Because I'm at 245 Bridge Street, and she's not even at my house, she's on campus, so I don't know why I said that."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:04:24-05:00",
      "duration": 21,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem. For the registration form, she'll be asked for a Rhode Island driver's license number or the last four digits of her Social Security number. If she has neither, she can still register, but she'd need to show ID later. At the polls she'd need to show a valid photo ID. A student ID from a college can work for that."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:04:45-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A student ID works? Even if it's from the school and not the state? Hold on, I'm in the car, I'm going to go through the"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:04:55-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hello? Ma'am?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:04:57-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "[line breaks up] Hello? Can you hear me now?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:05:01-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I think we lost you for a second. I'm here."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:05:05-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'm so sorry about that. The call dropped when I went under the bridge. Okay, I'm parked now. You said the student ID works?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:05:14-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. A student ID from a Rhode Island college is one of the accepted forms of photo ID at the polls. A regular driver's license, a passport, or a few other photo IDs also work. If hers is from an out-of-state school, I'd suggest she bring a second form, just to be safe."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:05:32-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hers is from the school here, so that should be fine. Um, and she can do the form online, or does she have to come in?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:05:42-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "She can do either. There's an online registration through the state, and there's also a paper form she can drop off or mail to us here at Canvassing. Our office is in City Hall."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:05:54-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, good. And is there a deadline? The next election, I mean."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:05:59-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There's a cutoff before each election, usually about a month out. I'd tell her to do it soon so she doesn't miss it. If she tells me which election she's aiming for, I can look up the date."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:06:13-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I think the one in the fall. She just turned eighteen, so this is her first time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:06:20-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Then she has plenty of time. She can register any time before the cutoff. I can also mail her a paper form if she'd like. Does she have a mailbox on campus?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:06:32-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "She does, I think, but I'll just tell her to do it online. That's easier. She'll do it tonight."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:06:39-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That works. Is there anything else I can help with?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:06:43-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, I think that's it. Dorm address is okay, student ID is okay, bring a second ID if it's from out of state. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:06:53-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Out-of-state school, yes. Hers is local, so she should be set. If she has any trouble with the form, she can call us back."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:07:02-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Great. Thank you, Walter. Sorry again about the call dropping."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:07:06-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No trouble at all. Have a good afternoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-18T12:07:10-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Bye."
    }
  ],
